WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.701
-Moving on,
we here at "Late Night"

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:06.200
don't always have enough time
to cover all of the recent news.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.968
So here with a recap
is one of our writers,

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.400
Amber Ruffin, in a segment
we call "Amber Says What."

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.434
-Hey.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.801
You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:20.234
Okay, first of all,

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:24.133
I heard 80-year-old actor
Robert De Niro just had a child,

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.701
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:30.167
Then I heard 83-year-old
Al Pacino also just had a child,

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.701
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:35.334
What old man is going
to have a toddler next, Seth?

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:41.000
-I do have a toddler.
-Gross. How?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.567
-The normal way.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.501
-Ew!

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.100
-Why don't you have a child?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.968
-Because I am a child.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.868
A sexy little child.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.501
[ Tink! ]

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.434
Then I heard that
they arrested Tupac's killer,

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:58.100
and I was like, "What...
is next on your to-do list?

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.567
Get a warrant
for John Wilkes Booth?"

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.133
You're late!

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.834
Why not figure out
who shot J.R.?

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.033
-Oh, it was Kristin Shepard.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.200
-You are so old.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.334
-I'm only five years
older than you.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.734
-I don't like this anymore.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:18.467
Then I heard that Ron DeSantis
wears secret high-heeled boots,

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:20.868
and I was like, "Wh-ha-ha-at?"

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:25.501
You must hate being short more
than you hate drag queens.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.033
Speaking of drag queens,
with those high heels,

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.367
you are one sew-in away

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.868
from violating
your own anti-trans bill, honey.

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:36.734
Then I read that all of
Trump's kids are testifying,

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.968
and I was like, "What?!"

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:42.200
Ivanka, Don Jr., Eric.

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.200
All the kids.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.901
Man, I think
he might go to jail.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.601
Now, I know, I know,
he may be rich,

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.434
he may be old,
and he may be a white man,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:57.334
but -- oops, never mind,
he will never go to jail.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:00.400
He'll probably just do what all
the other old guys are doing --

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.400
have a baby, which I believe
to be a prison in its own right.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.701
Okay, so then I heard En Vogue

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:11.234
is going to be in the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.367
I was like, "What?!"
And I have to say this.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.234
Please, NBC, corporate daddy,

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:20.534
you have to let me in
to see that.

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.868
Oh, Seth, do you have tickets
to the parade?

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:24.968
-No.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.300
-Then what is the point of you?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.801
Why are we doing this?

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.534
What is any of this for

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.434
if it's not going to help us
see En Vogue?

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.934
Then Britney Spears
released her memoir,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:39.167
"The Woman in Me," and spilled
the tea on Justin Timberlake.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.200
And I was like, "Wh-ha-aaaat?"

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.667
It's, like, a lot,

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.501
and I don't know if I'm allowed
to talk about what she said,

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.934
but let's just say this.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.701
Now, do you want to hear
some more gossip?

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.534
Okay, so,
Congressman George Santos

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:03.868
was running around his job
with a baby,

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.667
and I was like, "What?"

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:10.801
When asked if the baby was his,
he said, "Not yet."

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.601
Which brings us to a segment
called "Amber Says Why."

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:21.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.701
Now, George Santos said
this baby wasn't his yet.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:30.334
Why? Yet? Is that a threat?
And if so, to who?

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.133
To me? America?

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.767
Whoever's baby that is?
What?

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:37.367
Whose baby is that and why?

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.067
Why the baby, George?

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.968
Why did they give
their baby to you?

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.501
Did you trick somebody
and steal their baby?

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:44.901
Where did you get
that baby from?

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:48.100
Does it want to go back?
Did you ever give the baby back?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.200
Why the baby, George?
For what reason?

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.601
What purpose was the baby
supposed to serve?

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.534
And did it serve that purpose?

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:58.534
And why does that baby
look more qualified

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:01.133
to work in Congress than you?

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.100
This has been "Amber Says Why."

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.200
Then I read that Beyoncé's
"Renaissance" tour

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.434
made $579 million.

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:14.634
[ Audience cheers ]

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:15.734
Me too, man.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.167
It made so much money,

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:20.534
it literally boosted the economy
everywhere it went.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.434
I read that and I was like...

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:26.767
because I'm not about to mess up
the Beyoncé mute challenge.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.033
Mnh-mnh.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.167
Then I saw that Beyoncé
went to the premiere

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:34.000
of Taylor Swift's new movie,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.534
Beyoncé is not at
a Taylor Swift premiere.

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:40.467
A Taylor Swift premiere
is at a Beyoncé.

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:42.334
And I can't even imagine

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.567
what Beyoncé in a movie theater
looks like.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.701
Walking up to
the concession stand like,

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:51.000
"I will have the Sugar Babies
and a bottle of Cristal."

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.367
Then --

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:55.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.901
It came out so much worse.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:02.334
Then I heard there were
a million bedbugs in Paris,

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.601
and I was like, "Quoi?"

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:08.934
Then I found out Usher was doing
the Super Bowl halftime show,

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.067
and I was like, "What!"

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:13.667
Well, I guess I'm going to
have to cook him

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:16.667
a real big breakfast
that morning.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.133
Not because
I'm sleeping with him,

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:21.234
but because I had to take on
an extra job as Usher's cook

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:24.334
'cause the writers' strike
lasted five months.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.434
Then I found out the actors
were still striking,

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.601
and I was like, "What?"

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:30.133
Matter of fact, Seth,

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.701
how am I allowed to be
doing this right now?

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:35.234
-Well, late-night television
shows fall under a specific --

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.701
-Ohh! Shut up.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:41.167
Then I heard that genetic
testing company 23andMe

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:44.434
was hacked, and I was like,
"What...were you thinking

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.400
when you gave away all
your genetic information

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.934
to some random company?"

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:50.868
See, that's why
I never did 23andMe.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:53.534
Well, that and in case
I ever want to do a murder.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.734
I want to get away with it.

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:58.000
Then I heard
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.100
got kicked out
of the musical "Beetlejuice"

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.133
for getting felt up by some guy.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.033
And I was like, "What?!"

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.701
"Beetlejuice"?
More like "Some Like It Hot."

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:12.467
"Some Like It Hot,"
co-written by Amber Ruffin,

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:15.067
now on Broadway
at the Shubert Theatre.

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.601
Boebert, why would you guys
stay in your seats for that?

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.234
At least escape to the bathroom

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.133
and pretend
you're taking a whiz.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:28.200
"The Wiz,"
written by Amber Ruffin,

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.400
touring America and coming
to Broadway March 29th.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.767
Tickets available
at wizmusical.com.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:36.067
-Hey, Amber, why do you
keep interrupting this bit

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:37.734
to plug all
your Broadway musicals?

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:40.300
-Because the strike
took too long,

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.133
and I got to make money
to take care of this baby.

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:49.968
-Amber, is that your baby?

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:51.868
-Not yet.
[ Tink! ]

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.667
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:01.067
-Amber Ruffin, everybody.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:03.367
We'll be right back
with Rachel Maddow.

